## Topics Covered

### Hashing vs Encryption

Understand the difference between password hashing and encryption, how each works, and why the distinction matters during password recovery research.

### Online vs Offline

Compare attacks performed against authentication services with attacks performed locally against obtained password hashes or protected artifacts.

### Salts

Learn how salts protect password hashes against precomputed attacks and why every password should use a unique salt.

### Key Derivation Functions

Study password-focused KDFs such as Argon2, bcrypt, scrypt, and PBKDF2 and how their cost parameters affect password recovery.

### Password Entropy

Understand the size of a password's possible search space and how length, randomness, and character selection affect it.

### Password Strength

Examine why password length alone does not determine practical security and how predictable patterns can reduce effective security.

### Cracking Time

Study how password length, candidate space, hashing algorithm, KDF configuration, hardware, and attack strategy influence recovery time.

## Research Approach

The foundation section provides the terminology and concepts used throughout the rest of the repository.

The research workflow is:

```text
Understand the Protection
        ↓
Identify the Target
        ↓
Determine the Attack Model
        ↓
Select an Appropriate Technique
        ↓
Perform a Controlled Test
        ↓
Measure the Result
        ↓
Analyze the Security Impact
```

All practical testing should use self-generated data, intentionally vulnerable laboratory targets, CTFs, or systems for which explicit authorization has been obtained.
